# The developer build tree: two checkouts and a venv, fetched by ./setup.sh.
# This is the only directory this project ever writes into. ./install.sh builds
# in a temporary directory instead and leaves nothing here at all.
/work/

# Python bytecode, from running the helper scripts in place
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Editors and desktop environments
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Safety net, not housekeeping -------------------------------------------
# Nothing here writes these into the repository: captures go to
# ~/goodix-captures, test images and logs go to /tmp, the SELinux module is
# built in a temporary directory. The patterns exist because the cost of one
# mistake is uniquely high.
#
# A USB trace of this sensor is a fingerprint image. The TLS session uses a
# publicly known all-zero pre-shared key, so anyone who obtains the file can
# decrypt it. The same goes for a raw frame dump. See CONTRIBUTING.md.
*.pcapng
*.pcap
*.pgm
*.raw
otp.bin
